#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171830 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/id #uuid "91f986c6-c305-50eb-a5b7-36043279d128" :question/math-academy-id "e-9505" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_1$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_1$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v-2u+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_2$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ -u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_3$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term $v^2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{T}_1$ and $\\mathbf{T}_2$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171831 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/id #uuid "9779a982-2048-58e2-8a90-df2bcb366d96" :question/math-academy-id "e-9506" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 5u + v - 6, \\qquad y = 2u + 4v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171832 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "2ddc4e15-3729-5425-953c-1cb95edc201b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9508" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v+1 \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = 3u - v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{1}, \\qquad y = u + (\\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{-5})v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{0} \\, .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+(-5)+0 = -4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa1eb52d-5918-531a-847e-e7183292a357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295113} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7f88db-602f-5d13-bd76-b67013a04e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295114} {:answer/id #uuid "4921b728-e559-5950-b1e1-5d48b087121d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295115} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc8898e-b8a2-5834-92d5-7b2cacef4d9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295116} {:answer/id #uuid "62384ace-b84c-5e85-95f4-b664393de08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa7f88db-602f-5d13-bd76-b67013a04e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295114} :answer-field/id #uuid "9adf5d47-b90f-57ec-9563-b1300c861940" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7c49d1f-62c6-5240-9ecd-d0ff7b646237" :question/math-academy-id "q-124247" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 1-{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u(v-1) \\\\ u-1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}9 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f585c66-0570-5c00-9d93-8acb8a3e506e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295127} {:answer/id #uuid "ac90f967-da15-5704-9665-c9929cd922e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295128} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f73f23-5f24-5207-95b5-1a3853e0f1cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295129} {:answer/id #uuid "4456ce1b-97eb-545d-b767-dd68122091aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295130} {:answer/id #uuid "750596c5-9b6f-5472-a950-f0c1ea73740f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f585c66-0570-5c00-9d93-8acb8a3e506e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295127} :answer-field/id #uuid "482bb424-6613-54b7-891f-74ee4de3f263" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "111538d1-a3c4-5a8b-bb3b-b571c7d190d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-124253" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u-1 \\\\ {e}^{v}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v)\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the exponential term ${e}^{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "761e281b-e631-5212-a160-f8db9cbeaac5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295134} {:answer/id #uuid "38946076-2c0f-5674-80f6-7effeb0eb079" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295135} {:answer/id #uuid "269d906d-77b3-5906-989e-e1566c26e416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295136} {:answer/id #uuid "822087bb-8c5c-53ed-ba35-dc591995de18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295137} {:answer/id #uuid "8b254214-745b-583a-bc64-6e5f547d1b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b254214-745b-583a-bc64-6e5f547d1b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295138} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cbccf9-50b4-50d4-af0b-6b7102c9915e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2fbd649a-72ec-5c96-b929-3b7a8cd0013b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124259" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv+3,\\,y=-9u+cv+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ -9u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3 \\\\ -9u+4v+4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=1u+0v+3,\\,y=-9u+4v+4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+0+4=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be48af4-b946-5e8b-ab28-4f792a31a974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295141} {:answer/id #uuid "5e9d9ce5-d759-57bf-80a9-b7ceff4906fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295142} {:answer/id #uuid "f870ced9-0883-5ba8-8e7f-2d7ff9a791bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295143} {:answer/id #uuid "2180f3a8-6e9c-5b8a-af2d-60e6a57d55c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295144} {:answer/id #uuid "6d9683bb-89bc-5459-b095-601993cf9cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f870ced9-0883-5ba8-8e7f-2d7ff9a791bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295143} :answer-field/id #uuid "0df96ffa-72ad-5985-a938-cb8d42f45297" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42e18668-b4ac-5ec0-a619-27855b78e8aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-124261" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv-2,\\,y=u+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u+8v \\\\ u\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u+8v-2 \\\\ u+5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=6u+8v-2,\\,y=u+5\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=6+8+5=19.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62ccceb4-6067-5bce-b982-d96ab19ee9ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295162} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b35623-d326-5fb9-91ba-e8f93b1fe7db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295163} {:answer/id #uuid "ec74b222-bfdc-5fd9-9901-d062abb31c9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295164} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8d000c-d154-5174-9dc0-69d3a40286ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295165} {:answer/id #uuid "ac9ac776-4ed0-511c-a57a-d8c2c9d6502c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62ccceb4-6067-5bce-b982-d96ab19ee9ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295162} :answer-field/id #uuid "879f4cc5-b9a7-5a26-b6f3-bc229be46c40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94ef537c-d453-5e44-8027-fc902bea1259" :question/math-academy-id "q-124284" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=4v-u,\\,y=3v-7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v \\\\ 3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-1+4+0=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "373f8f6b-b1ad-57d5-ad02-6acbef1341c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295169} {:answer/id #uuid "8e14f16e-9b4e-58f1-906b-1eee902250fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295170} {:answer/id #uuid "38e23b92-2a75-5dfc-bdf4-513200c83294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295171} {:answer/id #uuid "1edbfb1c-9a04-5adb-89fb-bf120ffd3ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295172} {:answer/id #uuid "f61e3520-7d0e-5c7c-96cf-a5c357e7b01d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "373f8f6b-b1ad-57d5-ad02-6acbef1341c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295169} :answer-field/id #uuid "313376e7-eb16-55f0-8f6e-6a40eb0fdbb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb3e7867-83ca-5695-bc9b-8585b1f7a576" :question/math-academy-id "q-124285" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=5u-3v-2,\\,y=2u+v+7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ a & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v-2 \\\\ 2u+v+7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v-2 \\\\ 2u+v+7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+(-2)=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5492cc5-8266-527b-b2cf-8d5f5fdc432f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295183} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe44c9c-07b3-55d3-820f-f382ef124b60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295184} {:answer/id #uuid "521bba8c-2428-52ba-852a-ac6683eb7c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295185} {:answer/id #uuid "0441e29b-bd6e-54e6-9755-0a4053ddb78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295186} {:answer/id #uuid "2f0a6c11-c265-5864-bb98-df70fe7d2d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f0a6c11-c265-5864-bb98-df70fe7d2d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295187} :answer-field/id #uuid "03a507a4-26f1-59b0-af28-c13d74c534ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27624eaf-a41b-5122-b27f-be42134ea00b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124301" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=6u-v,\\,y=2u-3v+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & -1 \\\\ 2 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v+4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=6+(-3)+4=7.\n$$"}]}
